tags: device-wipe

A promise of the node: before it gives a device to an instance, it clears the device.
No data that an earlier instance wrote to the memory or to the state of the device stays
readable.

The value is empty. Any other value is not valid.

With no promise, the caller assumes that data of an earlier instance can stay on the
device. The node is bound.

=== formal
class=promise
name=device-wipe
rule=before the node gives a device to an instance, no data that an earlier instance wrote to the memory or the state of the device is readable
